  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-workspace",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -210,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "Conversation-first. Sidebar 248px collapsing to nothing, top bar 48px, reading column 792px, composer radius 16px. No permanent file tree, terminal, diff or preview, and no bottom status bar.\nFinished low-risk work collapses into one Working group with quiet rows; only the current action stays open. Permission requests, errors and anything needing attention stay expanded and stop execution behind them.\nModel lives in the composer, context and permission mode in its options menu, project and branch in the project menu.\nVerified with no horizontal overflow and WCAG AA contrast at 1920, 1440, 1366, 1024 and 768."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-onboarding",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Five steps in the same dark shell as the workspace, down from eleven light ones.\nStep 2 replaces the three equal recommendation cards with one recommended profile, a plain-language reason, and alternatives behind Compare other options. Model family, quantization and context stay behind Advanced.\nStep 3 folds runtime install, model download and the capability self-test into one screen; the seven technical checks sit behind View details.\nStep 5 is the real workspace, not a congratulations page."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-marketing",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Light surface. One primary Download action and one secondary See how it works; no fake prompt box in the hero.\nThe hero shows the actual dark workspace built from the same components and tokens as the app, not a placeholder panel. The three editorial sections alternate text with real interface, again built from live components rather than images.\nStill undrawn: Product, Model detail, Download, Pricing as a full route, Sign in, Account, Docs, Changelog."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-superseded",
      "page": "page-4",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 800,
      "text": "Do not build from this page.\nThe first six are the original three-panel IDE layout, replaced when the screen map locked the workspace as conversation-first. The ten light onboarding screens are replaced by the five-step dark flow.\nKept only because some content is worth porting: the recovery-state anatomy, the profile evidence table, the settings privacy pane and the cloud-boost consent screen."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
    "page": "page-1"
  }
}